<%#
  Standalone layout for the printable postal letter.

  WHY THIS EXISTS: the letter used to render inside "decidim/admin/users", so
  every print carried the admin chrome — the hamburger, the organisation name,
  "See site", the language switcher, the signed-in operator's e-mail address and
  the breadcrumb — onto paper that goes to a citizen. Worse, the admin layout's
  own wrapper margins shifted the page content, so the address block could never
  land where a window envelope expects it, and the extra height pushed the
  letter onto a second, near-empty page.

  A letter is not an admin screen. It gets its own document: no framework CSS,
  no navigation, nothing but the page itself, so the millimetre geometry below
  is the geometry the printer receives.
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= I18n.locale %>">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
    <title><%= t("decidim.bih.postal.admin.postages.printable_letter.title") %></title>
    <%# Installed into every host's public/ by Decidim::Bih::REQUIRED_PUBLIC_ASSETS.
        Falls back to the system stack if it is ever missing. %>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/mi/mi-fonts.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <%= yield %>
  </body>
</html>
